//! The owner's end of a pushed tenant config slice (tacplus#927,
//! sys/configpush.proto): the receiver a service that owns a tenant-scope
//! (spec.config_slice) with delivery CONFIG_SLICE_DELIVERY_PUSH serves, and
//! the holder its code reads the slice from.
//!
//! The generated ServiceManager builds a [`Receiver`] with the service's pushed
//! slices and serves it beside the service; the owner's code reads a slice
//! through the ServiceManager's typed accessor, never this crate. Every rule is
//! the receiver's, before the owner sees anything (the same rules as the Go and
//! Java receivers):
//!
//! - The caller is a tenant's record store, the subject
//!   spiffe://<td>/tenants/<tid>/services/stratum in this owner's own trust
//!   domain, and the owner's [`TenantRegistry`] holds <tid>. Anything else is
//!   PERMISSION_DENIED with no description, the reason in the log. A receiver
//!   with no TenantRegistry admits nobody (it fails closed).
//! - The first frame is a snapshot, or the stream ends FAILED_PRECONDITION.
//! - Every slice of a frame names one of the owner's pushed slices and its value
//!   decodes as the slice's message and passes its generated validation, or the
//!   stream ends INVALID_ARGUMENT and nothing of that frame is applied.
//! - A slice is held only at a version greater than the one held for (tenant,
//!   slice): an equal or lower one is acked STALE and changes nothing, and the
//!   stream stays open.
//!
//! It holds slices in memory only and never persists them: the owner has none
//! for a tenant until that tenant's first snapshot is accepted, and after a
//! restart every tenant's publisher sends its snapshot again. A slice it holds
//! stays when its stream ends, until a newer version or a restart.

